<!--
    Objective-C method signatures from SDK headers (`option objcsdk <dir>|off`).

    Issue: a selector stub `objc_msgSend$setAlpha:` has a prototype only when
    something in the image declares the selector, and a UIKit setter never
    does, so its calls kept the untyped call-site inference: on ios_kcm 2,897
    of 25,084 stub calls rendered with no argument at all
    (`objc_msgSend$setHidden:();`), `setAlpha:` showed the bit pattern of its
    double in an integer slot, and `setFrame:` passed one garbage word for a
    CGRect. The declarations exist in the SDK the app was built against; Apple
    headers may not ship with kuna, so they are read at load from a directory
    the user names.

    Stage / sub-stage: P1 external-refinement. `analyzers/objc/kuna_objcsdk.rs`
    reads `@interface`/`@protocol` bodies (methods, `@property` getter/setter
    pairs honouring `getter=`/`setter=`/`readonly`) and `typedef`s, encodes each
    declaration the way the runtime metadata would (`v@:d`), and the stub
    prototype path pins the arguments: an HFA struct (`CGRect`) is spread over
    `d0..d3` as `arg_x, arg_y, arg_width, arg_height`, a struct return is the
    flat `CGRect` the model places in `d0..d3`.

    P0 assertion: `option objcsdk <directory>|off` (an env-bridged load-time
    setting, so it is set BEFORE the `load file` it applies to and cleared at
    the end so the harness process carries nothing into the next test).

    The fixture is `macho_objc_sdk.m`: `Widget` declared and never implemented,
    every send a linker stub; `tests/fixtures/objc_sdk/Widget.h` is a
    hand-written header (no Apple text) declaring the same selectors.

    Pass 1 (`objc on`, no headers) reproduces the BUG: `setAlpha:()` with no
    argument, `setFrame:(v1,a1._0_16_,a2 + 10.0,a3)`, an `undefined16` first
    parameter.
    Pass 2 (`objc on`, `objcsdk` pointed at the header directory) is the FIX:
    `setAlpha:(a1,a0)` with its double, `setTag:(a1,a3)`, `isHidden(a1)`,
    `v1 = objc_msgSend$frame(a1)` as a `CGRect`, `setFrame:` with the four
    members, `insertSubview:atIndex:(a1,a2,a3)`; the stub itself is
    `CGRect objc_msgSend$frame(objc_object *self)`.
-->
